I think la selpa'i has perfectly responded to the question, but I have an=
=20
objection about the English interpretation of {ka}, and a complement to the=
=20
explanation about relation of {ka} and other abstractors.

Le lundi 13 juillet 2015 21:45:58 UTC, selpa'i a =C3=A9crit :
>
>
> One reason why {lo ka} even crops up in these places is that people try=
=20
> to avoid having to repeating sumti, the {ka} is supposed to auto-insert=
=20
> the sumti for them, but this causes problems when using {ka} in places=20
> where you don't want the {ce'u} to be "filled", where you don't want the=
=20
> {ka}-property to be applied to any outside sumti. {nelci} is such an=20
> example. {mi nelci lo ka limna} could mean "I like the property of=20
> swimming", "I like swimmingness", without any indication or claim that=20
> the speaker is swimming.=20



{mi nelci lo ka limna} means rather "I like property of swimmer", not=20
"swimming". {ka} (property) signifies a special case of {si'o} (idea,=20
concept) in Lojban.

Both {lo si'o broda} and {lo ka broda} signify =C2=AB signified =C2=BB (mea=
ning) of=20
predicate {broda}. The difference is that a sentence in {ka}-clause has=20
only one sumti place blank (denoted with {ce'u}), while a sentence in=20
{si'o}-clause has all places blank. {si'o}-{ka}-{du'u} forms full set of=20
predicate abstraction.

lo si'o (ce'u) limna (ce'u) :=20
idea, concept of swimming ; idea, concept that is signified by a predicate=
=20
"X swims in fluid Y."

lo ka (ce'u) limna (zo'e) :=20
property of swimmer ; property that is signified by a predicate "X swims in=
=20
some fluid," "X has property of swimmer in some fluid."

lo ka (zo'e) limna ce'u :=20
property of swimming fluid ; property that is signified by a predicate=20
"someone swims in fluid Y," "Y has property of fluid in which someone=20
swims."

lo du'u (zo'e) limna (zo'e) :=20
=C2=AB signified =C2=BB of a predicate "someone swims in some fluid."

lo se du'u (zo'e) limna (zo'e) :=20
=C2=AB signifying =C2=BB (string of symbols) of a predicate "someone swims =
in some=20
fluid."

mu'o

